<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:57:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Africa CDC calls crisis meeting as Ebola spreads</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4eb0c0472151a95f3060715620c999320e6e8eb0e70033d881ece9e96948fd4</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-cdc-calls-crisis-meeting-as-ebola-spreads/a-79728604--521b9bc7db1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-cdc-calls-crisis-meeting-as-ebola-spreads/a-79728604?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">African health officials will hold a crisis meeting as the Ebola outbreak spreads from Congo to neighboring countries and beyond. The "extraordinary virtual meeting" will convene on October 28.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Austrian, Swiss women kidnapped in Niger are freed — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71ce94e01079dd512003803a1d63cfb618dee75d8ba6c4c4e60a38eeac843fa0</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T02:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austrian-swiss-women-kidnapped-in-niger-are-freed-report/a-79727419--97b94dcfa335.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austrian-swiss-women-kidnapped-in-niger-are-freed-report/a-79727419?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An Austrian woman and a Swiss woman kidnapped in Niger have been freed after 18 months in captivity, local reports say.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case, in capital Abuja</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26f0df0e40ca06fa598fa5a76da0ac9ea2669564949f275b54dd4750b8cfccd4</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377--c6985b1c776f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-in-capital-abuja/a-79717377?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has reported its first known case of Ebola during Africa's latest outbreak originating in the DRC. Health Minister Muhammad Ali Pate said the patient was a woman who had recently flown to Abuja from Uganda.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Tinubu Must Go!': Nigeria's northern protests test limits of political dissent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67de2340351693439c60ac10c604d7a9bb7bfdd5dba0c0bd981fbaff399bf7f6</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tinubu-must-go-nigeria-s-northern-protests-test-limits-of-political-dissent/a-79713785--b9a2ff0fa9c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tinubu-must-go-nigeria-s-northern-protests-test-limits-of-political-dissent/a-79713785?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of several men wearing anti-government T-shirts and the disruption of a political meeting have renewed debate over free expression and protest rights in Nigeria.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The Bundestag has debated the genocide Germany carried out in Namibia a century ago. But will it spur progress on addressing colonial crimes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c477e34308c700faf0daf5d419a9d9bf68c7d190824ad5c55afdacb0d9efc41c</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:55:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur/a-79682388--50aa326f1793.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bundestag-has-debated-the-genocide-germany-carried-out-in-namibia-a-century-ago-but-will-it-spur-progress-on-addressing-colonial-crimes/a-79682388?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties have forced a debate in the Bundestag on the early-20th-century genocide Germany carried out in Namibia. Will this finally spur progress in addressing colonial crimes?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
